<Base title="Privacy" description="How Modern Software handles project enquiries and information submitted through this website."><article class="prose wrap"><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</span><h1>Your information.</h1><p>When you submit an enquiry, Modern Software uses your name, contact information and project details to respond, discuss requirements and manage any resulting business relationship.</p><h2>Where your enquiry goes</h2><p>Enquiries are delivered by SendGrid to Glen’s business-managed email inbox. The website is hosted on Vercel. These providers process information needed to operate the service and may process it outside the UK under their applicable terms and safeguards.</p><h2>What to share</h2><p>Provide only what is needed to explain your enquiry. Do not submit passwords, financial account details or confidential information about customers.</p><h2>Keeping information</h2><p>Enquiry correspondence is kept while needed to respond, manage the relationship and meet applicable record-keeping obligations. Enquiry contacts are not added to a marketing list automatically.</p><h2>Website storage</h2><p>The public marketing pages do not load advertising or analytics trackers. Private administration tools use Firebase authentication and related browser storage to manage signed-in access.</p><h2>Questions and requests</h2><p>For questions, access, correction or deletion requests, email <a href="mailto:glen.adamson@modern-software.co.uk">glen.adamson@modern-software.co.uk</a>. You can also raise a concern with the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p></article></Base>
